    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s action with a targeted offensive approach centered on capitalizing against softer pitching matchups. **Brady House** stands out as our highest-rated play at a 63.81, largely due to a lucrative matchup against Woods Richardson (xERA 4.85). The combination of a favorable park factor and a solid #5 spot in the order gives him the highest ceiling of the day. **Nasim Nunez** (62.09) is effectively tied for that top tier; while his #9 lineup spot is a drag on his raw production, the significant edge against Woods Richardson\u2019s xERA makes him an essential piece of our daily efficiency strategy. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** (69.76) remains a pillar of the lineup; despite facing the tougher arm in Max Meyer, his #1 order spot and a positive dynamic platoon split provide the floor necessary to anchor our SS position.\n\nThe toughest decision of the morning involved the exclusion of **Coby Mayo**, who sat just shy of our threshold with a 38.03 score. While **Coby Mayo** possesses the power profile we covet, the combination of a projected #8 batting order and the difficulty of facing Max Meyer forced him to the bench in favor of the higher-upside matchups provided by **Jacob Wilson** and **Josh Jung**. We are keeping a close watch on **Liam Hicks** (42.93) and **Jackson Merrill** (59.87); both are impacted by \"Lineup Pending\" designations and, in **Jackson Merrill**'s case, a challenging dynamic platoon split against the left-handed Matthew Liberatore. These remain the primary risk factors for our current build, though we feel confident in the remaining active roster as we navigate the scarcity of our stolen base targets.",
